{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>First interpretation</b><br>תִּשׁוּרִי (you look). Like אֲשׁוּרֶנּוּ (I see him); and it is not [from a root meaning] near." "<b>Second interpretation</b><br>And now, come with me from Lebanon — so why do you look down at me from a high place, and frighten me from coming to you, as though there were a lion's den there?" "<b>Third interpretation</b><br>From Lebanon: those who come on foot." "From the peak of Senir: even from across the Jordan." "From lions' dens: even when they come on pilgrimage and they are outside the Land — in the land of the uncircumcised, who are compared to lions and leopards — all will come, and the nations will not be able to prevent them or harm them."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The bracketed כמו appears in the Hebrew source as an editorial gloss indicating a comparison; retained as bracketed.", 4 "The bracketed clause in the Hebrew source appears to be an editorial interpolation; translated as integral to the sentence."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:19.348979907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}